The user is asking me to create a storyworld design packet - chunk 1 of what appears to be a game/story design inspired by Romeo and Juliet set in Sana'a, Yemen. This involves creating encounters between Sunni and Shia characters navigating family conflict.

Let me construct the JSON with exactly 8 encounters (c01_01 through c01_08), each with 3 visible options, with a secret_option only on c01_04. The chunk should cover:
- first glimpse
- family boundary  
- shared text/poem
- secret clue that the feud is being managed by rumor
- first choice to meet or retreat

I need to output exactly one JSON object between BEGIN_STORYWORLD_PACKET and END_STORYWOLD_PACKET markers.

Let me construct this carefully with ASCII-only characters, valid JSON syntax, and respecting all constraints.
BEGIN_STORYWORLD_PACKET
{
  "title": "The Two Balconies of Sana'a",
  "subtitle": "A storyworld where love meets inherited grievance",
  "about": "Romeo and Juliet set in Sana'a between a Sunni boy and a Shia girl. Rami al-Hakimi, a calligrapher's son, and Zahra al-Mutawakkil, a doctor's daughter, fall in love while their families, neighborhood councils, checkpoints, clerics, and friends make every private choice public.",
  "characters": [
    {"name": "Rami al-Hakimi", "role": "Sunni boy, apprentice calligrapher, impulsive but morally serious"},
    {"name": "Zahra al-Mutawakkil", "role": "Shia girl, medical student, sharp observer, unwilling to be reduced to symbol"},
    {"name": "Layla", "role": "Zahra's cousin, practical mediator with divided loyalties"},
    {"name": "Yasin", "role": "Rami's friend, poet and rumor-runner who can inflame or repair"}
  ],
  "variables": [
    {"name": "Secrecy_Disclosure", "description": "whether love, violence, and bargains stay hidden or become accountable"},
    {"name": "Family_Truce", "description": "whether family honor hardens into feud or opens toward negotiated truce"},
    {"name": "Sectarian_Trust", "description": "whether religious identity becomes threat, bridge, or shared vocabulary"},
    {"name": "Love_Duty", "description": "whether private love escapes duty, transforms it, or is crushed by it"}
  ],
  "encounters": [
    {
      "id": "c01_01",
      "act": "act1",
      "title": "First Glimpse at the Friday Market",
      "description": "Rami carries ink jars through the old souq. A woman in navy headscarf pauses before his father's calligraphy shop, tracing letters with her eye.",
      "options": [
        {"text": "Watch from behind the doorframe", "next": "c01_02", "profile": "veil"},
        {"text": "Step forward and greet her", "next": "c01_02", "profile": "disclosure"},
        {"text": "Lower your head and pass by quickly", "next": "c01_03", "profile": "order"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "c01_02",
      "act": "act1",
      "title": "The Name on the Street",
      "description": "She turns. You see her clearly now. A neighbor passes, slows slightly, looks between you both. The air tightens.",
      "options": [
        {"text": "Ask: What do you seek at this shop?", "next": "c01_03", "profile": "witness"},
        {"text": "Say nothing. Let silence bridge the distance.", "next": "c01_04", "profile": "spirit"},
        {"text": "Turn away before anyone can speak of this.", "next": "c01_05", "profile": "identity"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "c01_03",
      "act": "act1",
      "title": "A Shared Verse at the Copyist's Stall",
      "description": "Days later, you find her at a copyist's stall in Bab al-Yemen. She holds a small book of pre-Islamic poetry. Her finger rests on a line about two stars that cannot meet.",
      "options": [
        {"text": "Recite the next verse with her", "next": "c01_04", "profile": "transmission"},
        {"text": "Ask who gave her this book", "next": "c01_05", "profile": "reason"},
        {"text": "Step back. This is not your place.", "next": "c01_06", "profile": "precedent"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "c01_04",
      "act": "act1",
      "title": "The Boundary Line on Bab al-Yemen",
      "description": "Yasin approaches, grinning. He says he's heard someone speak of the al-Hakimi boy and an al-Mutawakkil girl meeting at the copyist's stall. His eyes dance.",
      "options": [
        {"text": "Tell him nothing happened", "next": "c01_05", "profile": "veil"},
        {"text": "Ask how he heard anything of it", "next": "c01_06", "profile": "community"},
        {"text": "Challenge him: Who else has spoken?", "next": "c01_07", "profile": "justice"}
      ],
      "secret_option": {
        "text": "Ask what Yasin plans to do with the story",
        "next": "c01_08",
        "profile": "disclosure",
        "unlock_condition": "Player has chosen a 'witness' or 'transmission' option previously"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "c01_05",
      "act": "act1",
      "title": "The Father's Warning",
      "description": "Your father calls you to the shop. He does not look at you as he speaks of how the al-Mutawakkil family has never trusted them, and how trust, once broken, takes generations to mend.",
      "options": [
        {"text": "Listen and say nothing", "next": "c01_06", "profile": "order"},
        {"text": "Ask what broke the trust between families", "next": "c01_07", "profile": "reason"},
        {"text": "Say: I do not carry their grievance", "next": "c01_08", "profile": "mercy"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "c01_06",
      "act": "act1",
      "title": "Layla at the Well in Bab al-Sha'b",
      "description": "You meet Zahra's cousin Layla by accident near the old well. She knows you from school. She speaks of how her cousin is being watched, how girls from their family must be careful.",
      "options": [
        {"text": "Ask if she will help convey a message", "next": "c01_07", "profile": "community"},
        {"text": "Tell her you mean no harm to anyone", "next": "c01_08", "profile": "mercy"},
        {"text": "Leave before she sees too much of your face", "next": "c01_end_retract", "profile": "identity"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "c01_07",
      "act": "act1",
      "title": "The Checkpoint at Night",
      "description": "You pass a neighborhood checkpoint late. The guards exchange glances as your name is called out. Someone recognizes you.",
      "options": [
        {"text": "Give your name and wait", "next": "c01_08", "profile": "witness"},
        {"text": "Claim you are visiting a sick friend", "next": "c01_end_retract", "profile": "veil"},
        {"text": "Ask what they want from you", "next": "c01_end_retract", "profile": "justice"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "c01_08",
      "act": "act1",
      "title": "First Choice: Meet or Retreat?",
      "description": "The pattern is clear now. Eyes follow you. Names are mentioned in passing. A note has been passed to Zahra through Layla, asking for one meeting at the old fountain behind Al-Azhar Mosque.",
      "options": [
        {"text": "Go to the fountain alone", "next": "chunk_02_entry", "profile": "disclosure"},
        {"text": "Send Yasin to ask if Layla can meet instead", "next": "chunk_02_entry_safe", "profile": "community"},
        {"text": "Write back that this must wait until the families are ready", "next": "c01_end_retract", "profile": "order"}
      ]
    }
  ]
}
END_STORYWORLD_PACKET
